Thumbs.db
Thumbs.db:encryptable
ehthumbs.db
ehthumbs_vista.db
*.stackdump
[Dd]esktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
*.cab
*.msi
*.msix
*.msm
*.msp
*.lnk

# Linux
*~
.fuse_hidden*
.directory
.Trash-*
.nfs*

# ==========================================
# Logs & Temporary Files
# ==========================================
*.log
logs/
*.tmp
*.bak
*.swp
*.swo
*~.nib
*.orig
*.rej

# ==========================================
# Knowledge Base
# ==========================================
# knowledge/ is tracked — contains destilled project knowledge

# Source documents (DSGVO: live in Obsidian vault, not in public repo)
antrag.md
handreichung.md

# ==========================================
# IDE & Editor Files
# ==========================================
# Sublime Text
*.sublime-workspace
*.sublime-project

# Atom
.atom/

# Emacs
*~
\#*\#
/.emacs.desktop
/.emacs.desktop.lock
*.elc
auto-save-list
tramp
.\#*

# Vim
[._]*.s[a-v][a-z]
[._]*.sw[a-p]
[._]s[a-rt-v][a-z]
[._]ss[a-gi-z]
[._]sw[a-p]
Session.vim
Sessionx.vim
.netrwhist

# ==========================================
# Build & Distribution
# ==========================================
node_modules/
package-lock.json
yarn.lock

# ==========================================
# GitHub Actions
# ==========================================
# GitHub Actions artifacts (don't ignore workflows)
!.github/workflows/

# ==========================================
# Project-Specific
# ==========================================
# Reports a pipeline run reproduces from the versioned XLSX. The quality
# snapshot stays tracked, it is the status communication for third parties.
data/reports/validation-report.md
data/reports/exploration-report.md

# Testing outputs
tests/outputs/
tests/*.html

# ==========================================
# Comments & Notes
# ==========================================
# Tracked: scripts, tests, documentation, the knowledge base, the vocabulary,
# the source XLSX under data/google-spreadsheet/, and the published artefacts
# under docs/ that GitHub Pages serves.
#
# Not tracked: credentials, IDE and OS files, virtual environments, the raw
# Google Drive backups under data/backup/ (they may carry personal data), and
# any report a pipeline run reproduces.
